Building GnuTLS (and its dependencies) for MSVC on ARM64
========================================================

TigerVNC's optional GnuTLS support needs a GnuTLS that MSVC can link.
There isn't one to download: vcpkg's port is marked

    "supports": "!windows | mingw"

so a Windows triplet legitimately contains no gnutls.lib, and that
absence is not evidence that anything is broken.

The ShiftMediaProject forks carry Visual Studio solutions for the whole
stack, but ship Win32 and x64 configurations only. These patches add
ARM64. They are recorded here because working them out again costs a
day, not because TigerVNC needs them -- nothing in this directory is
part of the build.


What the patches apply to
-------------------------

Each was generated against, and verified to apply cleanly to, these
commits:

    zlib     6c46b96   v1.3.1-2-g6c46b96
    gmp      6702eddd  6.2.1-4-4-g6702eddd0
    nettle   f73aec48  nettle_3.10.1_release_20241230-1-gf73aec48
    gnutls   5995f0dc  3.8.8-1-g5995f0dc5

from github.com/ShiftMediaProject/{zlib,gmp,nettle,gnutls}, plus
vsyasm-arm64.patch for github.com/ShiftMediaProject/VSYASM.


What they change
----------------

Most of it is msbuild: adding Debug|ARM64 and Release|ARM64 (and the
DLL, WinRT and DLLStaticDeps variants where a solution has them) beside
the existing Win32 and x64 entries, and excluding the x86 assembly from
ARM64 builds in the *_files.props.

The parts that are not msbuild are worth knowing about, because they are
where the actual porting is:

  gmp/longlong.h
      <immintrin.h> is x86/x64 only and is a hard #error on ARM64;
      <intrin.h> already provides the _BitScan* intrinsics used there.
      _umul128 is x64 only, so umul_ppmm is implemented with __umulh
      plus an ordinary 64-bit multiply for the low half.

  gmp/SMP/config.h
      This fork ships no aarch64 assembly, so the HAVE_NATIVE_mpn_*
      block is disabled on ARM64. Leaving it declared makes gmp skip its
      own portable C and then fail to link.

  gmp/SMP/gmp.h
      __aarch64__ / _M_ARM64 added to the 64-bit limb detection.

  nettle/SMP/config.h
      Same story: no assembly on ARM64, so the generic C paths are used.

  gnutls/SMP/config.h
      PadLock is a VIA x86 instruction-set extension. It does not exist
      on ARM64 and its sources are excluded from that build.

  VSYASM install_script.bat
      The installer does not recognise an ARM64 host, so SYSARCH is
      never set and it fails. The x64 yasm runs under emulation there.

      Do NOT patch yasm.props to accept ARM64 targets: yasm has no
      ARM64 output format, so mapping ARM64 to -f win64 makes it emit
      x86-64 objects that cannot link. An earlier version of these
      patches did exactly that; the visible symptom is orphaned x86-64
      .obj files in the ARM64 output directory. The stock "not
      supported on this platform" error is correct. The gmp project
      files must exclude every YASM item on ARM64 instead -- if any
      slip through, check the COFF machine type of the objects rather
      than trusting a green build.


Using them
----------

Clone each fork at the commit above, apply the matching patch, then
build in dependency order -- zlib, gmp, nettle, gnutls -- with the
ReleaseDLL|ARM64 configuration. Collect the headers, import libraries
and DLLs into one tree, and point TigerVNC at it:

    cmake -S . -B build -G "Visual Studio 17 2022" -A ARM64 \
      -DGNUTLS_INCLUDE_DIR=<tree>/include \
      -DGNUTLS_LIBRARY=<tree>/lib/gnutls.lib

VSYASM has to be installed before building gmp or nettle, from an
elevated prompt, or the assembler custom build step is unavailable.

These are a record of one working build, not a supported product. If
ShiftMediaProject has moved on, expect to redo rather than rebase them.
